<h4>Core attack loop (excerpt)</h4>
<pre>rec = 1 - cos(dummy_grad, true_grad)          # direction match (Geiping 2020)
loss = rec + tv_weight * total_variation(dummy)
loss.backward(); opt.step()                   # optimise the IMAGE, not the model
# label recovered analytically from sign of last-layer gradient (iDLG)</pre>

<h2>6&nbsp;&nbsp;Preliminary Evaluation, Limitations and Plan for IA-2</h2>
<h3>6.1&nbsp;&nbsp;Observations</h3>
<ul>
<li>The attack reliably recovers the label (analytic, deterministic) and a
high-fidelity image for a single untrained-network sample.</li>
<li>Reconstruction quality is seed-sensitive; restarts + median consensus
materially stabilise it.</li>
<li>Evaluation measures adopted: MSE, PSNR, SSIM (structural) and LPIPS
(perceptual) for reconstruction; accuracy/AUC and TPR@low-FPR for membership
inference; achieved &epsilon; for the DP guarantee.</li>
</ul>
<h3>6.2&nbsp;&nbsp;Known limitations (to address in IA-2)</h3>
<ul>
<li>Single-image regime is the easiest case; batch reconstruction is harder and
is being extended (sizes 1&rarr;4&rarr;8).</li>
<li>LeNet has no BatchNorm, so the strongest known prior (BN-statistics matching)
is not yet used; a BN variant is planned as an ablation.</li>
<li>Defences are evaluated on this model scale; generalisation to deeper networks
is discussed, not exhaustively measured.</li>
</ul>
<h3>6.3&nbsp;&nbsp;Plan for IA-2</h3>
<ol>
<li>Complete the four-defence privacy&ndash;utility sweep and the membership-inference
DP audit (empirical vs analytical &epsilon;).</li>
<li>Cross-validate the hand-written attack against the published <i>breaching</i>
framework.</li>
<li>Add the malicious-server contrast (Robbing-the-Fed) analytically.</li>
<li>Assemble the final technical report and an IEEE-format paper draft.</li>
</ol>

<h2>7&nbsp;&nbsp;Individual Contribution Statement</h2>
<p>All code, experiments, figures and analysis in this submission are my own
individual work. My specific contributions are: (i)&nbsp;the unified
attack&ndash;defence benchmark design that measures four distinct syllabus
defence families against a single gradient-inversion attack &mdash; a comparison
not previously assembled in one study; (ii)&nbsp;a from-scratch implementation of
the cosine+TV+iDLG attack with restart-median group consistency;
(iii)&nbsp;the privacy&ndash;utility evaluation protocol spanning reconstruction
metrics and membership-inference auditing; and (iv)&nbsp;the full reproducible
pipeline and documentation. External references are cited in Section&nbsp;8.</p>

